  "explanation": {
    "event_selection": "Only events in the authoritative list were selected. All controllable events required for the object and zone search, approach, claim, pickup, and drop are included: search_object, claim_red, claim_green, claim_blue, approach_object, pick_up_object, search_zone, approach_zone, drop_object. Zone and object observations for all colors and claim resolution observations are included. No motion-plant low-level commands, communication commands unrelated to the task, or obstacle/skip/unrelated colors are present.",
    "transition_design": "The automaton models a single round delivery for any object color, branching at visible-object observation. In searching_object, the robot waits for a visible object, then enters the appropriate claim-<color> attempt state. If it wins (claim_<color>), it begins approaching (approach_object self-loops). If it loses (received_claim_<color>), it returns to search. Object approach can be interrupted by <color>_object_not_visible (reverts to color-locked search), or return to approach on <color>_object_visible. If the object is reached, the robot can pick up and transition to searching for the corresponding zone. Zone search/approach/recovery follow the same pattern—search_zone or approach_zone self-loops, <color>_zone_visible switches to approach, <color>_zone_not_visible returns to search, and <color>_zone_reached enables drop_object and the mission is marked delivered. Each branch advances only on the required observations, ensuring ordered protocol and no mixing of colors or invalid transitions.",
